WEBVTT

00:11.130 --> 00:13.080
Want to go somewhere during summer break?

00:13.080 --> 00:13.750
Yeah.

00:13.750 --> 00:15.000
Yeah, that sounds good.

00:19.790 --> 00:22.000
I want to see Airi-chan again.

00:22.500 --> 00:25.000
Huh? Um, sorry. What did you say?

00:25.290 --> 00:27.580
I said I want to play with Airi-chan again.

00:27.580 --> 00:29.130
She was so cute, you know?

00:29.460 --> 00:31.920
For some reason she pounced on me, though.

00:31.920 --> 00:33.540
Sorry about that.

00:34.080 --> 00:35.130
She was so cute!

00:35.630 --> 00:37.960
Hey, aren't you going to invite Sajo?

00:38.420 --> 00:40.830
Although lately, you two haven't been together often.

00:41.170 --> 00:45.420
Maybe it's gotten harder for him to start a conversation,
since Natsukawa-san has gotten so popular.

00:46.040 --> 00:47.420
It's that, or...

00:47.580 --> 00:49.130
I wonder if something happened.

00:49.250 --> 00:49.960
What?

00:50.580 --> 00:54.130
Well, he used to be like way too much,
but that stopped suddenly.

00:55.540 --> 00:57.330
I-I wonder why...

00:57.920 --> 00:58.790
You know?

01:02.210 --> 01:04.630
I guess people do notice after all, huh...?

01:20.000 --> 01:23.960
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

01:20.000 --> 01:23.960
<b>is a Realist</b>

01:24.210 --> 01:29.670
With a command from the sky that's peeking out,
we hold onto our feelings as we depart

01:29.670 --> 01:34.380
Even though our eyes meet,
we're swayed by the wind into a roundabout way

01:35.460 --> 01:40.920
A dream snapshot taken by the blink of the eyes;
the memories adorn my heart

01:40.920 --> 01:46.380
It seems I like these times; even though they're frustrating

01:47.420 --> 01:52.290
Staying away then getting closer; a dream I'd started to give up on

01:52.540 --> 01:57.960
The day I can land that well; I want to try chasing after that

01:57.960 --> 02:03.380
The sky is filled up with the things that can't be all conveyed

02:03.540 --> 02:09.170
For some reason, the change in countenance
of your true feelings was at odds

02:09.170 --> 02:17.460
Even though I might get lost, the sky always had two heartbeats

02:17.460 --> 02:19.960
I've told you many times

02:20.130 --> 02:26.170
If these youthful feelings are joined together,
I wonder what kind of view will spread out

02:26.170 --> 02:30.830
I want to know that colorful feeling

02:37.630 --> 02:40.750
<b>Should We Open It? Should We Open It? Should We Look Inside?</b>

02:43.380 --> 02:45.580
So, that's "Aika Natsukawa"...

02:45.790 --> 02:48.460
She does stand out, just as rumored.

02:48.710 --> 02:50.540
I think she could be of use.

02:51.000 --> 02:52.040
Huh...?

02:52.380 --> 02:54.130
What do you want with Natsukawa?

02:54.380 --> 02:55.790
Eek!

02:57.540 --> 02:59.080
Wh-who are you!?

02:59.330 --> 03:02.330
Could you please not call out suddenly from behind!?

03:03.250 --> 03:06.830
Just who do you think I am?

03:07.670 --> 03:10.580
Unlike you, I come from an aristocratic-

03:10.580 --> 03:13.210
For an aristocrat, you gave out an amusing shriek.

03:13.210 --> 03:13.830
What!?

03:13.920 --> 03:15.540
"Eek!"

03:17.380 --> 03:19.250
H-hey you!

03:19.250 --> 03:21.330
Marika-san would never do something like-

03:21.580 --> 03:23.330
"Eek!"

03:23.630 --> 03:26.580
How rude of you. And this is how
these West side people are like.

03:26.920 --> 03:29.210
Let us go! He is not even worth engaging in.

03:29.210 --> 03:31.130
Honestly, how rude!

03:31.130 --> 03:32.330
Let's hurry up and go.

03:34.380 --> 03:35.960
What's all the noise about?

03:35.460 --> 03:38.670
Marika-san, a guy like that should just be pitied.

03:36.920 --> 03:38.670
What happened, Sajotchi?

03:38.670 --> 03:39.830
Oh, well, some kind of...

03:40.130 --> 03:42.080
Trio of strange pampered ladies were...

03:40.130 --> 03:42.080
Yes, that was an unexpected thing.

03:43.130 --> 03:44.750
A "trio of pampered ladies"?

03:44.750 --> 03:47.710
I'm just saying there are some
strange people in the world...

04:07.380 --> 04:08.130
Whoa!

04:09.080 --> 04:10.710
Wh-why are you here?

04:10.880 --> 04:13.750
Oh. Uh, morning, Natsukawa.

04:14.880 --> 04:16.960
Isn't it kind of cold today?

04:16.960 --> 04:19.420
What? Y-you think so...?

04:20.960 --> 04:22.500
Maybe it's just my imagination.

04:22.750 --> 04:23.380
Oh!

04:23.580 --> 04:24.960
H-hey!

04:26.880 --> 04:28.920
Jeez, what's up with him...?

04:29.380 --> 04:30.920
Huh? What's wrong-

04:30.920 --> 04:32.040
Natsukawa!

04:32.540 --> 04:33.040
Huh!?

04:34.920 --> 04:35.540
What!?

04:41.960 --> 04:43.040
What the...!?

04:43.880 --> 04:44.670
Oh!

04:50.000 --> 04:52.580
Even dripping with water, I'm drop-dead gorgeous.

04:53.250 --> 04:55.420
Whoa. Even your eyes and face
look like you're dead inside.

04:55.960 --> 04:58.080
Could you not deliver the final blow?

04:58.920 --> 05:00.170
It's not my day.

05:01.210 --> 05:01.920
Here.

05:02.420 --> 05:03.040
Huh?

05:03.210 --> 05:06.880
I-I haven't used it yet, so use this and dry yourself.

05:07.210 --> 05:09.710
What? That's okay, plus I'd feel bad.

05:10.290 --> 05:11.290
I-it's fine!

05:13.330 --> 05:14.460
Wanna use this too?

05:14.670 --> 05:19.920
Whoa! That stinks! It seriously stinks!
It reeks of sweat! And it's used!? Give me a break...

05:20.250 --> 05:21.040
Oh...!

05:24.500 --> 05:25.460
Huh!?

05:25.880 --> 05:29.080
Huh? He fell asleep? Is he asleep? No way.

05:29.080 --> 05:30.580
Did he fall asleep too easily?

05:29.290 --> 05:31.290
Hey. Tap, tap.

05:30.960 --> 05:33.130
Hey... I heard a really loud noise.

05:33.790 --> 05:36.130
You know, I'm not asleep yet...

05:34.170 --> 05:35.880
Aichi, should we let him sleep?

05:35.880 --> 05:37.130
Hey! Is he asleep?

05:37.460 --> 05:39.130
Wataru? Hey...

05:41.130 --> 05:48.830
The French Revolution was a bourgeois revolution
that occurred between 1789 through 1795.

05:48.830 --> 05:49.580
Oh!

05:49.920 --> 05:56.170
Crap. I legit fell asleep... World History...
It's already 3rd period, huh...?

05:57.250 --> 06:00.580
I'm going to play innocent and pretend
that I've been awake since earlier.

06:02.130 --> 06:07.710
Oh! This is actually one of those bad ones.
My headache hurts. My headache hurts.

06:08.170 --> 06:09.380
Tap, tap.

06:09.790 --> 06:11.960
Sajotchi... You wake up?

06:11.960 --> 06:12.750
Ugh...

06:12.960 --> 06:13.750
Oh!

06:14.750 --> 06:17.380
So, you're finally awake, Sajo-kun.

06:19.040 --> 06:22.000
I was told about the circumstance
regarding your sweat outfit look.

06:22.290 --> 06:24.830
Now, I can understand why you'd feel like sulking,

06:24.830 --> 06:28.130
but that doesn't give you an excuse
to abandon your lessons, right?

06:28.580 --> 06:29.540
Yes ma'am.

06:30.170 --> 06:30.880
Um...

06:30.880 --> 06:32.630
Huh? What is it?

06:32.960 --> 06:35.500
I-is it okay if I go to the infirmary?

06:37.250 --> 06:41.290
Yes, that's fine. Have someone
show you their notes later.

06:41.290 --> 06:42.040
Okay...

06:46.630 --> 06:47.420
Whoa!

06:48.290 --> 06:49.000
Oh!

06:49.130 --> 06:50.540
What the!? Sajotchi!?

06:53.830 --> 06:56.000
Is he okay? Oh no!

06:54.080 --> 06:57.670
Sajo-kun, are you okay? Sajo-kun!?

06:56.000 --> 06:57.670
You okay!? Hey!

07:02.130 --> 07:04.710
You know, I guess it turns out you are an interesting guy.

07:06.330 --> 07:09.380
When I started 2nd-year in middle school,
that was the first time I put up a front.

07:10.290 --> 07:12.670
I was not to completely disclose my true feelings.

07:13.170 --> 07:16.580
I was to assume an attitude and have
a sarcastic way of looking at things.

07:17.210 --> 07:19.750
I thought that was what becoming
an adult was supposed to be like...

07:20.460 --> 07:23.330
Sajo, over here! C'mon, hurry up.

07:23.710 --> 07:25.330
Okay. I'm coming right now!

07:26.500 --> 07:27.420
Whoa!

07:43.710 --> 07:44.790
You okay?

07:49.580 --> 07:53.080
<b>Infirmary</b>

07:50.420 --> 07:53.080
Oh my, so that's how he collapsed.

07:53.710 --> 07:55.330
That's a showstopping performance.

07:55.710 --> 07:57.960
"Performance"...? Sensei.

07:58.170 --> 08:03.580
It doesn't seem like he hit his head,
and although he has a fever, well, he should be okay.

08:04.330 --> 08:05.960
He's still asleep, but...

08:06.290 --> 08:07.500
Do you want to go look in on him?

08:07.790 --> 08:08.670
Yes.

08:10.080 --> 08:11.000
Yes!

08:17.210 --> 08:19.330
It's unexpectedly the first time
seeing his sleeping face, right?

08:19.830 --> 08:20.630
Yeah...

08:22.040 --> 08:23.670
You're worried.

08:23.670 --> 08:25.250
Th-that's-

08:25.250 --> 08:28.500
Alright now. Classes are going to start about now.

08:28.960 --> 08:30.750
Return to your classroom.

08:30.880 --> 08:32.830
Oh... Sorry.

08:37.000 --> 08:38.330
He'll be okay.

08:46.920 --> 08:49.290
Oh... Uh... Dammit!

08:50.580 --> 08:52.170
Oh, are you awake?

08:52.580 --> 08:53.830
Oh, uh...

08:53.830 --> 08:57.920
You collapsed in the classroom,
and everyone carried and transported you here.

08:58.830 --> 09:02.000
Right... Do I have a cold?

09:02.210 --> 09:06.420
Well, when I took your temperature earlier,
it was 38.6 degrees Celsius.

09:02.210 --> 09:06.420
<b>Note: 38.6 Celsius = 101.5 Fahrenheit</b>

09:06.420 --> 09:08.170
It still might go up higher after this.

09:08.750 --> 09:13.500
Seriously...? But I was totally fine up until this morning.

09:13.880 --> 09:16.290
Maybe it's one of those situations
where your tension gave out?

09:16.290 --> 09:18.460
You were probably already tired all along.

09:18.830 --> 09:20.040
Tired...

09:20.670 --> 09:22.790
That includes psychological kinds as well.

09:23.580 --> 09:24.330
Here.

09:24.330 --> 09:25.210
Oh...

09:25.540 --> 09:27.000
You should sleep for a little while longer.

09:27.210 --> 09:28.130
Okay...

09:46.130 --> 09:48.210
Why am I thinking this much about him...?

09:49.830 --> 09:51.330
Hey look! Isn't that...?

09:51.330 --> 09:52.330
No way! OMG! Wow!

09:52.710 --> 09:54.210
Shinomiya-senpai!

09:54.380 --> 09:55.250
<b>Morals &</b>

09:54.380 --> 09:55.250
<b>Discipline</b>

09:54.580 --> 09:56.670
Wow! She's so cool...

09:57.500 --> 09:58.380
Hey there!

09:58.380 --> 10:01.960
Let's see... It was Ashida-san, right?

10:01.960 --> 10:05.170
Y-yes! I-it's been a while.

10:05.420 --> 10:07.460
I had business with Sajo, but...

10:07.750 --> 10:09.420
Oh... Well...

10:09.710 --> 10:10.750
Actually...

10:14.380 --> 10:15.540
He collapsed?

10:15.750 --> 10:16.750
Yeah...

10:17.210 --> 10:20.880
That's... Most likely that hasn't been conveyed to Kaede.

10:20.880 --> 10:23.080
Um, one more time, for Sajotchi...

10:24.380 --> 10:26.920
We were thinking of paying a visit to Sajo-kun, but...

10:27.250 --> 10:29.830
Should we inquire upon his condition or something...?

10:30.670 --> 10:35.460
No... After I let Kaede know,
I'm thinking that we'll head over too.

10:35.460 --> 10:36.830
Oh, okay!

10:37.630 --> 10:38.630
Thank you.

10:43.630 --> 10:45.380
Huh? Wh-what da!?

10:46.210 --> 10:48.380
Well, you've admired her for some time, right?

10:48.380 --> 10:50.880
Yeah... Why're you pinching me!?

10:56.750 --> 11:00.580
Huh!? It's light! Sajotchi's book bag is super light!

11:01.000 --> 11:03.130
Hey, don't be too rough on-

11:03.130 --> 11:03.960
Here!

11:05.960 --> 11:08.380
Oh... It really is light.

11:08.830 --> 11:11.380
Should we open it? Should we open it?
Should we look inside?

11:11.580 --> 11:14.330
Jeez, we can't do that to someone's
stuff without permission.

11:14.330 --> 11:17.420
We wouldn't like it if things
like naughty books came out, right?

11:17.670 --> 11:19.170
Th-there's no way...

11:21.290 --> 11:22.710
Are there any, maybe?

11:22.710 --> 11:24.880
Thump, thump, heart's pounding.

11:25.290 --> 11:27.000
I'm telling you; we're not looking!

11:29.540 --> 11:31.750
We're not gonna look? Really?

11:31.750 --> 11:32.580
Not looking!

11:32.580 --> 11:33.880
But that's a shame!

11:34.040 --> 11:38.040
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

11:34.040 --> 11:38.040
<b>is a Realist</b>

11:41.540 --> 11:45.040
<b>Infirmary</b>

11:43.000 --> 11:44.790
Excuse us!

11:45.460 --> 11:46.170
Huh?

11:52.250 --> 11:54.380
Sajotchi, are you awake?

11:54.380 --> 11:55.210
Shh!

11:55.210 --> 11:55.790
Huh?

11:55.790 --> 11:57.290
Shh...

11:58.920 --> 12:00.540
Surely, he's asleep, right?

12:00.880 --> 12:01.790
Yeah...

12:02.460 --> 12:03.670
I wonder if he's okay.

12:04.880 --> 12:05.670
Oh!

12:12.170 --> 12:15.830
C-c'mon. If you're awake, then you should answer.

12:16.290 --> 12:17.210
Yeah...

12:18.290 --> 12:19.460
You can't sleep?

12:20.000 --> 12:20.790
No...

12:21.420 --> 12:22.750
You want anything?

12:24.540 --> 12:25.830
We've got a Pokari.

12:30.630 --> 12:31.460
Sorry...

12:31.460 --> 12:32.210
What?

12:32.500 --> 12:33.750
For causing trouble.

12:33.750 --> 12:35.040
That's not...

12:36.290 --> 12:38.710
What's wrong? You're kinda being weird.

12:39.500 --> 12:40.540
Like what?

12:40.540 --> 12:42.330
"Like what?", uh...

12:43.750 --> 12:44.670
Yeah.

12:58.500 --> 12:59.250
Ow!

12:59.710 --> 13:01.000
W-Wataru!?

12:59.960 --> 13:01.000
Sajotchi!

13:01.710 --> 13:03.580
Sorry. It's my headache...

13:05.830 --> 13:07.790
Y-you don't have to talk...

13:08.000 --> 13:09.130
Don't touch me!

13:09.130 --> 13:09.920
Oh!

13:10.290 --> 13:11.880
Wh-why!?

13:14.170 --> 13:15.630
I don't want to pass my cold on...

13:16.500 --> 13:18.130
You know, to like Airi-chan...

13:18.130 --> 13:21.710
Huh? Oh... O-okay...

13:22.750 --> 13:24.750
I don't want her to suffer, so...

13:27.130 --> 13:28.750
<b>Infirmary</b>

13:27.380 --> 13:31.880
Hey! C'mon! What the!? What's up with that!? With that!

13:32.130 --> 13:35.420
A weakened vulnerable Sajotchi. A Sajotchi like that is...!

13:35.750 --> 13:39.040
N-no, stop that. It's inappropriate, or rather...

13:39.710 --> 13:42.750
You know it's not like we paid him
a visit with that in mind...

13:43.790 --> 13:45.540
What's going on, you two?

13:45.540 --> 13:47.080
Shinomiya-senpai!

13:45.710 --> 13:47.080
Big Sister!

13:47.460 --> 13:48.880
S-sorry.

13:48.880 --> 13:50.920
We were waiting for the two of you!

13:50.920 --> 13:52.210
I-I see.

13:52.790 --> 13:53.790
And him?

13:53.790 --> 13:55.420
Oh, um...

13:58.420 --> 13:59.790
Oh, it's you, Big Sis.

14:00.710 --> 14:01.670
How're you doing?

14:02.080 --> 14:03.250
Head hurts.

14:03.580 --> 14:04.710
And that you collapsed?

14:04.710 --> 14:05.790
I'm okay.

14:08.130 --> 14:09.040
Idiot.

14:17.080 --> 14:18.040
Let's see...

14:19.170 --> 14:20.540
It's cold...

14:21.460 --> 14:24.830
Is there anything you want? I'll go buy it for you.

14:25.330 --> 14:30.540
I'm going to go call mom, since you probably
haven't done anything like contact her anyway.

14:30.790 --> 14:31.830
We'll be right back.

14:34.830 --> 14:36.330
Wata... Oh...

14:46.580 --> 14:49.830
Morning, everyone. I'm starting homeroom!

14:50.210 --> 14:51.330
Sajo-kun...

14:51.830 --> 14:53.540
is absent. Okay.

14:59.630 --> 15:02.630
<b>Colds - Aches, Cough, Fever, Runny Nose</b>

14:59.630 --> 15:02.630
<b>Recovers Well</b>

15:05.380 --> 15:06.170
Oh!

15:09.290 --> 15:10.250
Huh!?

15:10.250 --> 15:12.250
N-Natsukawa!? Ashida!

15:12.750 --> 15:14.130
You finally answered!

15:14.420 --> 15:16.290
By any chance, were you sleeping?

15:18.380 --> 15:19.630
How nice of you to come.

15:19.920 --> 15:22.630
"How nice of you to come."? Don't even go there!

15:22.630 --> 15:24.080
<b>Sajo</b>

15:22.630 --> 15:24.080
<b>You know, to be alive is wonderful.</b>

15:22.630 --> 15:24.080
<b>What's up with that?</b>

15:22.630 --> 15:24.080
<b>Aika</b>

15:22.630 --> 15:24.080
<b>What's wrong?</b>

15:22.630 --> 15:24.080
<b>Class Rep</b>

15:22.630 --> 15:24.080
<b>You alive?</b>

15:23.000 --> 15:26.630
You know, if you're going to make a joke,
then express the joke like you're kidding around.

15:24.080 --> 15:26.630
<b>Aika</b>

15:24.080 --> 15:26.630
<b>What's wrong?</b>

15:24.090 --> 15:26.630
<b>Class Rep</b>

15:24.090 --> 15:26.630
<b>You alive?</b>

15:24.090 --> 15:26.630
<b>Zakiyama</b>

15:24.090 --> 15:26.630
<b>Did he die?</b>

15:24.090 --> 15:26.630
<b>Mattsu</b>

15:24.090 --> 15:26.630
<b>Huh? For real?</b>

15:27.170 --> 15:30.080
Yeah, you had one brief comment,
and then no response after that.

15:30.080 --> 15:30.960
What...?

15:31.630 --> 15:34.630
<b>Colds - Aches, Cough, Fever, Runny Nose</b>

15:31.630 --> 15:34.630
<b>Recovers Well</b>

15:35.080 --> 15:37.540
Whoa...! Unread messages in the triple digits...

15:37.920 --> 15:39.670
<b>Zakiyama</b>

15:37.920 --> 15:39.670
<b>Did he die?</b>

15:37.920 --> 15:39.670
<b>Mattsu</b>

15:37.920 --> 15:39.670
<b>Huh? For real?</b>

15:38.290 --> 15:40.130
"My bad, I was sleeping."

15:38.330 --> 15:39.670
<b>My bad, I was sleeping.</b>

15:39.670 --> 15:40.920
<b>Did he die?</b>

15:39.670 --> 15:40.920
<b>Mattsu</b>

15:39.670 --> 15:40.920
<b>Huh? For real?</b>

15:39.670 --> 15:40.920
<b>My bad, I was sleeping.</b>

15:40.920 --> 15:41.920
<b>My bad, I was sleeping.</b>

15:40.920 --> 15:41.920
<b>Mattsu</b>

15:40.920 --> 15:41.920
<b>Huh?</b>

15:41.920 --> 15:42.920
<b>Mattsu</b>

15:41.920 --> 15:42.920
<b>Huh?</b>

15:41.920 --> 15:42.920
<b>Zakiyama</b>

15:41.920 --> 15:42.920
<b>Stay asleep forever.</b>

15:42.920 --> 15:43.920
<b>Zakiyama</b>

15:42.920 --> 15:43.920
<b>Stay asleep forever.</b>

15:42.920 --> 15:43.920
<b>Iwata</b>

15:42.920 --> 15:43.920
<b>Don't wake up.</b>

15:44.130 --> 15:45.080
Uh-oh...

15:45.630 --> 15:47.080
You brought this on yourself!

15:47.080 --> 15:50.130
You know, Aichi's the one who
suggested we go pay you a visit.

15:50.130 --> 15:51.460
H-hey, Kei!

15:51.790 --> 15:53.960
Oh! Seriously?

15:54.710 --> 15:58.170
W-well, the reason you got drenched was because...

15:58.170 --> 15:58.880
Huh?

16:02.920 --> 16:04.710
N-never mind!

16:05.210 --> 16:07.960
Aichi, I'm glad you knew where Sajotchi's house was.

16:07.960 --> 16:08.670
Oh!

16:09.170 --> 16:12.630
I-it's that Yamazaki-kun told me previously, that's all.

16:12.630 --> 16:13.500
Uh-huh.

16:15.250 --> 16:16.630
You know, thanks.

16:19.790 --> 16:21.330
W-we're leaving now, Kei!

16:21.330 --> 16:22.750
What!? You're leaving already?

16:23.130 --> 16:25.960
Since we found out you're okay,
that's good enough, right?

16:26.290 --> 16:27.580
Oh, you sure?

16:28.290 --> 16:30.420
Okay then, here. A get-well present.

16:30.420 --> 16:31.040
Okay...

16:32.000 --> 16:35.170
You don't have to see us out!
Just make sure to lock up afterwards!

16:35.630 --> 16:37.170
Oh, okay.

16:44.500 --> 16:46.540
You're here again? What do you want?

16:46.670 --> 16:48.580
That is because no matter how much
time passed, you wouldn't... Oh!

16:50.920 --> 16:52.420
Aika Natsukawa-san!

16:52.880 --> 16:54.670
I have something to tell you!

16:55.040 --> 16:57.540
Um... Wh-what is it?

16:58.330 --> 17:01.710
In addition to having excellent grades
as being ranked second in our class year,

17:01.710 --> 17:04.130
and even though it is said that
you are just a little adorable...

17:08.080 --> 17:10.380
You really are adorable.

17:10.380 --> 17:13.630
What? Um... Thanks.

17:13.960 --> 17:18.960
S-since you are just a little excellent,
and as I am the top of the class year,

17:18.960 --> 17:22.830
I, Claudine Marika Shinonome,
grant you the privilege of supporting me.

17:23.580 --> 17:24.460
Huh...?

17:26.380 --> 17:27.750
Why don't you support her?

17:27.750 --> 17:29.290
What? Um...

17:29.670 --> 17:31.250
K-keep it up!

17:32.710 --> 17:37.330
No, no, no! That is not it! That is not what I meant!

17:37.540 --> 17:38.330
What...?

17:38.750 --> 17:44.460
Natsukawa-san! For me! You will support me in order
for me to become the next Student Council President!

17:44.670 --> 17:49.210
What? Can a 1st-year even become
the Student Council President?

17:49.830 --> 17:51.380
I will explain.

17:51.830 --> 17:57.830
<b>Student Council Room</b>

17:52.460 --> 17:54.580
For all of the roles of the Student Council,

17:54.580 --> 17:57.710
regardless of class year, self-nomination or
by recommendation, one can run as a candidate.

17:58.170 --> 18:00.210
Way to go! The walking student handbook.

18:01.330 --> 18:05.130
K..Kaoruko-san. That probably was
not a compliment, you know?

18:05.380 --> 18:10.210
Ahem! That being said, in general,
1st-year students are at a disadvantage.

18:10.380 --> 18:14.790
There is the trend that upper level students are the ones
who become the representatives of the students.

18:14.790 --> 18:16.250
Well, that's true.

18:16.670 --> 18:19.750
Or rather, if one were to consider
the natural course of things,

18:19.750 --> 18:21.460
then wouldn't the next Student Council President be
Kai-senpai?

18:21.630 --> 18:27.420
No, that is something he himself has been denying,
and the present situation among the 2nd-years,

18:27.420 --> 18:30.710
is that there is no one who has announced
they will be running as a candidate for President.

18:31.210 --> 18:34.750
Nevertheless, when the time comes,
there will be candidates that appear.

18:35.130 --> 18:39.710
I must therefore gather willing supporters by that time.

18:41.460 --> 18:44.880
In other words, you want
Natsukawa as a poster girl, right?

18:44.880 --> 18:47.580
It could be said like that, but...

18:48.210 --> 18:49.790
No, that's a bad move.

18:49.790 --> 18:50.960
What was that!?

18:52.000 --> 18:56.630
I believe I heard a somewhat questionable phrase.
May I ask the reason why?

18:59.040 --> 18:59.710
Uh...

19:03.960 --> 19:06.250
Natsukawa stands out too much.

19:06.250 --> 19:06.920
Huh!?

19:07.540 --> 19:10.380
Clau... Was it Claumati-san?

19:10.710 --> 19:12.040
Huh!? "Clauma..."?

19:12.460 --> 19:16.540
If you use Natsukawa as a poster girl,
then everyone is going to think this for sure:

19:16.830 --> 19:20.290
"So, it's not Natsukawa-san, but
that person who's running as a candidate?"

19:20.290 --> 19:22.210
H-how rude!

19:29.040 --> 19:32.710
If you'll allow me to say this as an average boy;
if you incorporate Natsukawa into this,

19:32.710 --> 19:35.000
then you yourself are going to be upstaged instead.

19:35.250 --> 19:36.960
Wh-what do you mean by that?

19:39.380 --> 19:41.210
Natsukawa is cuter than you.

19:41.210 --> 19:41.880
Huh!?

19:46.830 --> 19:49.040
Please excuse me.

19:52.670 --> 19:53.880
How dare you...

19:53.880 --> 19:54.830
Marika-san!

19:54.830 --> 19:55.500
Oh!

19:55.710 --> 19:58.000
Huh!? What's with her? What's going on?

19:58.000 --> 19:59.130
For this time...

19:59.130 --> 20:01.170
It may be better to back off.

20:02.710 --> 20:05.920
I will take my leave for this time. Just for this time!

20:06.380 --> 20:07.750
Yes. Well then, another time.

20:07.750 --> 20:08.420
Hmpf!

20:08.580 --> 20:09.790
O-okay...

20:09.790 --> 20:11.420
Sajotchi, Sajotchi.

20:11.420 --> 20:12.380
Huh?

20:14.580 --> 20:15.420
What?

20:16.460 --> 20:18.920
Huh? What? What's up with her?

20:19.290 --> 20:21.960
Sajotchi, it's because you said
something out of this world.

20:22.170 --> 20:23.500
"Out of this world"...?

20:23.830 --> 20:25.670
You said Aichi was cute.

20:28.040 --> 20:31.250
But for Natsukawa, that's something she's sick and
tired of hearing she probably wants her ears burned off.

20:31.250 --> 20:34.420
I've repeatedly said that many times before, so why now?

20:34.580 --> 20:36.830
Well, when you say it that confidently, then...

20:37.040 --> 20:40.460
Also, it's like time, place and
circumstances all lined up, so to speak.

20:40.460 --> 20:43.130
So, in a different sense, her ears are burning, you know?

20:45.500 --> 20:47.880
Sajotchi, so it's like that, okay?

20:47.880 --> 20:48.750
What!?

20:50.330 --> 20:54.630
Don't go around saying something so embarrassing!
You still haven't gotten over your cold, right!?

20:57.920 --> 20:59.000
So cute...

20:59.210 --> 21:02.210
What!? D-d-d-d...

21:02.210 --> 21:04.080
Don't look at me!

21:28.580 --> 21:31.040
So annoying! Or so it seems, right?

21:31.330 --> 21:34.580
Aw! I wish I hadn't said that...

21:35.420 --> 21:41.540
But you know, why're you suddenly making
that curt face towards me...?

21:43.250 --> 21:45.460
A text that's been left on read and abandoned

21:45.460 --> 21:47.750
But there are replies if it’s a group text, kind of thing

21:47.960 --> 21:49.920
I thought we were close, but then you became distant

21:50.170 --> 21:51.710
Why am I this lonely?

21:51.710 --> 21:53.630
You're not going to chase after me, today?

21:53.630 --> 21:55.170
I wish I could be honest with myself

21:56.630 --> 22:02.960
That's because it's the first time
I learned there's such a heartrending feeling...

22:02.960 --> 22:04.380
And yet, hey!

22:04.380 --> 22:05.920
Why're you going away??

22:05.920 --> 22:07.670
Why is it a secret!?

22:07.880 --> 22:10.040
I'm full of frustration and...

22:10.040 --> 22:11.420
Oh! Oh!

22:11.420 --> 22:13.130
I can't say something like this

22:13.130 --> 22:17.080
But earlier those weren't my true feelings

22:17.080 --> 22:18.460
Let that get through to you

22:18.540 --> 22:20.170
Why do I get angry...?

22:20.170 --> 22:21.710
I can't be cute...

22:21.710 --> 22:24.170
You don't like me anymore...??

22:24.330 --> 22:27.040
Oh! Oh! Oh, oh!

22:29.040 --> 22:30.000
Why?

22:30.670 --> 22:31.960
Don't hate me

22:35.040 --> 22:36.420
...Listen, "You see...!"

22:41.040 --> 22:47.040
<b>Summer break is here!!</b>

22:41.040 --> 22:47.040
<b>We're gonna totally have fun!</b>

22:41.040 --> 22:47.040
<b>Go study!!!</b>

22:41.330 --> 22:43.670
With summer break before their very eyes,
for high school students,

22:43.670 --> 22:47.040
the necessary thing to moderately
improve one's standard of living is...

22:47.040 --> 22:48.710
Yes, it is the yen.

22:48.960 --> 22:52.330
This has that feel of somewhat trying to make do
with a certain sum of money, and it's kinda cool.

22:52.670 --> 22:55.330
I'll also acquire some real-world experience,
so this'll kill two birds with one stone.

22:53.040 --> 22:55.790
<b>STAFF Wanted!!</b>

22:53.040 --> 22:55.790
<b>Age & experience - no questions asked.</b>

22:53.040 --> 22:55.790
<b>A person who likes books!!</b>

22:53.040 --> 22:55.790
<b>Hourly pay 1,100 yen</b>

22:53.050 --> 22:55.790
<b>Work hours 10 AM ~ 3 PM</b>

22:53.050 --> 22:55.790
<b>*Training included</b>

22:53.050 --> 22:55.790
<b>For more details, please ask the staff!!</b>

22:53.050 --> 22:55.790
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

22:55.460 --> 22:58.630
I kept on looking online and in the classifieds,
and this is the place that I found.

22:55.960 --> 22:57.130
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

22:56.830 --> 22:58.210
<b>Used books</b>

22:56.830 --> 22:58.210
<b>- Buy & Sell</b>

22:58.210 --> 23:00.290
<b>We buy</b>

22:58.210 --> 23:00.290
<b>used books.</b>

23:00.290 --> 23:02.210
You sure you're okay with this?

23:02.540 --> 23:03.790
It's enough.

23:04.040 --> 23:10.540
<b>STAFF Wanted!!</b>

23:04.420 --> 23:06.920
But it can't be that good of an hourly pay.

23:07.290 --> 23:10.330
No, you see, it's not like I want
an overabundance of pocket money.

23:13.670 --> 23:17.880
I'll do the purchase assessments,
price tag stickers and inventory control.

23:17.880 --> 23:20.630
So then, can I count on you to keep the
books organized and deal with the customers?

23:20.630 --> 23:22.540
If anything, are you sure that's all you need me to do?

23:22.540 --> 23:25.960
Oh no, if you can deal with the customers,
that would be a godsend.

23:26.290 --> 23:27.250
"A godsend"....

23:29.920 --> 23:34.580
I see, "a godsend," huh?
It appears he's well versed in this field too.

23:37.710 --> 23:38.960
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

23:38.960 --> 23:41.040
<b>Used books</b>

23:38.960 --> 23:41.040
<b>- Buy & Sell</b>

23:40.170 --> 23:41.040
<b>We buy</b>

23:40.170 --> 23:41.040
<b>used books.</b>
